# `Predicate`, `Consumer`, `Supplier`

## The three "something's missing" shapes

```java
Predicate<String> isBlank = s -> s.isBlank();   // test → boolean
Consumer<String>  print   = s -> System.out.println(s);  // side effect → void
Supplier<Double>  random  = () -> Math.random();  // no input → produce
```

- **`Predicate.test`** — `filter`, `removeIf`
- **`Consumer.accept`** — `forEach` (act, don't compute)
- **`Supplier.get`** — lazy/deferred value: `orElseGet(...)`

## Variants

- **`Bi…`** = two inputs — `map.forEach(BiConsumer<K,V>)`
- **`Int…`/`Long…`/`Double…`** = primitive, no boxing

## Pick by shape

| Interface | In → Out | Use |
|---|---|---|
| `Supplier` | — → `T` | lazy value |
| `Consumer` | `T` → — | side effect |
| `Predicate` | `T` → `boolean` | a test |
| `Function` | `T` → `R` | transform |
